{
  "id": "ss.lib.dot-head",
  "name": "Dot's head",
  "description": "Dot's head, drawn on its own and large, to be composed into `ss.char.dot` by `use` at about a fifth of this size. From the neck up: a ribbed gaiter into a steel seal ring with a latch on each side, and the top of the mantle collar with its frost edge. Over that a helmet dome shaded in a radial gradient from a steel highlight at the upper left down to slate in shadow, with a seam over the crown, a riveted jaw guard, a brow ridge, and on the near side a cheek plate and a slatted breather with its valve. The visor is curved black glass — a radial gradient with a cold frost tint laid over it, two reflection streaks and one hard blue glint — framed in dark steel, and behind it on the far side an ear cover with a ring and a dead-blue core. Over all of it a deep hood: cloth in a linear gradient from light at the crown to near-black at the hem, a shadow band inside the opening so the visor sits recessed, a steel-grey rim, stitching along the rim, creases in the cloth, and the hood's point trailing back. Two steel mounts at the crown, through the hood, take the feelers — the first inch of each is here; the long dead arcs that hang from them belong to the character document, where they can be animated. No skin anywhere.",
